WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:04.550
A thrilling new teaser trailer for upcoming
Disney+ series The Mandalorian has arrived,

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:08.520
and it gives us our first look at Ming-Na
Wen's mysterious assassin character.

00:00:08.929 --> 00:00:13.220
The 30-second clip consists mostly of previously
seen footage – including sweeping looks

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:18.010
at the Outer Rim's landscapes and the Mandalorian's
weaponry and clothes, as well as a few of

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:20.680
the creatures, ships, people, and battles
he'll face.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:24.680
At one point in the new teaser trailer, the
Mandalorian appears before a group of aliens

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:25.400
and humans.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:29.760
Among them is Carl Weathers' Greef Carga,
whom we know works with the Mandalorian and

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:31.140
heads up a bounty hunter guild.

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:35.700
The trailer also sees the return of several
scout troopers on speeder bikes, plus the

00:00:35.719 --> 00:00:41.120
Taika Waititi-voiced IG-11 rapidly spinning
and unleashing a burst of plasma energy shots

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:41.740
around it.

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:46.079
The crowning moment of the new Mandalorian
teaser trailer, however, is a brief but punchy

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:51.070
exchange that sees Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.
actress Ming-Na Wen deliver a single, goosebumps-inducing

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:52.660
line to the titular character.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:55.680
"Your name will be legendary."

00:00:56.380 --> 00:01:00.640
It's a funny nod to the fan-favorite villain-esque
Boba Fett, who wore almost identical armor

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.540
to the new Disney+ series character.

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:07.720
But, as showrunner Jon Favreau has clarified,
Fett wasn't an actual Mandalorian and Pedro

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:09.160
Pascal's character is.

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:14.020
Up to this point, not much has been revealed
about Ming-Na Wen's character, Fennec Shand.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:17.600
In an interview with Vanity Fair, Wen revealed
several details about her role.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:21.960
Wen described the gun-toting mercenary as
similar to Han Solo in that she starts with

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:24.240
no beliefs in any causes but her own.

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:25.280
According to Wen:

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:27.540
"We got our inspiration really from the name.

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:29.680
The idea of a fennec fox came to mind.

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:31.760
I just love that whole image with the name."

00:01:32.009 --> 00:01:36.119
Fennec's original concept design apparently
gave her a more disheveled look, but she appears

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:38.800
in the new Mandalorian trailer as much more
put-together.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:43.060
That's due to Wen, who had a hand in shaping
her character's appearance to be more fitting

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:44.080
of the fox imagery.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:44.960
Wen said:

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:49.300
"At first, the idea was maybe just have her
hair be loose, unkempt kind of thing.

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:53.360
'And I thought, well, she's going to be wearing
a helmet and she's this stealth assassin.

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:57.020
How great would it be if her hair has a bit
of the fennec fox architecture to it?'

00:01:57.380 --> 00:02:01.030
So the hairstylist came up with this great
braiding system, that just gives an idea of

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:02.229
these triangular points.

00:02:02.229 --> 00:02:03.260
Like her ears."

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:07.719
Due to the darkness of the shot in the trailer
in which Fennec appears, you can't quite see

00:02:07.719 --> 00:02:12.120
the more intricate elements of Fennec's hairstyle,
but Wen revealed that her braid will be threaded

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:15.700
with orange strands as a callback to her character's
fox inspiration.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:18.620
Expect her outfits to feature these color
elements as well.

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:19.580
According to Wen:

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:23.780
"The designer, Joseph [Porro], came up with
this amazing outfit that I fell in love with

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:24.540
right away.

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:27.420
It's black, but then there's the fennec orange
punch to it.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:29.580
So that's kind of like her brand, I guess."

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:33.720
While we've got a peek at Fennec Shand now,
fans will have to wait a bit to see her make

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.560
her first appearance on The Mandalorian.

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:39.731
Wen confirmed that her character and the Mandalorian
aren't slated to cross paths until around

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:40.900
halfway through the first season.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:45.799
On the upside, the new trailer for The Mandalorian
did manage to deliver more about another previously

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:49.920
teased character, voiced by Nick Nolte: an
Ugnaught named, uh...

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:51.340
Quill?

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:52.680
Koo-will?

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:54.520
Kanye?

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:59.960
Anyway, past previews have offered silent
glimpses of the alien riding a blurrg - a

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:04.409
two-legged creature that looks sort of like
a fish-dinosaur hybrid - but this is the first

00:03:04.409 --> 00:03:05.760
time we've heard this guy talk.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:10.810
The Mandalorian, the first live-action Star
Wars TV show, also stars Giancarlo Esposito

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:15.939
as interstellar administrator Moff Gideon
and Gina Carano as former Rebel Shock Trooper

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:16.660
Cara Dune.

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:22.080
Plus, Werner Herzog as an imperial agent,
Bill Burr as a bounty hunter, and Julia Jones

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:24.840
as a character presently known only as Omera.

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:27.520
The Disney+ series will premiere on November
12.

